---
source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_plain(&refusal)
---
safix: the mapping 'router' is keepassxc-to-safix, so the database is where its value comes
from, and the database holds no entry at 'safix/bob/router'. Nothing was written.

safix does not author that entry, and this is the one place the asymmetry
shows: a value the operator types into their own database is theirs to
create, where a value safix mints is safix's. Create it, and the next run
converges safix onto it.

If safix is the producer after all, the mapping is declared the wrong way
round: mode = "safix-to-keepassxc" makes the database follow safix.
